{
  "title": "5: al-Maaedah المائدة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَوْفُوْا بِالْعُقُوْدِ ؕ اُحِلَّتْ لَكُمْ بَهِيْمَةُ الْاَنْعَامِ اِلَّا مَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ غَيْرَ مُحِلِّى الصَّيْدِ وَاَنْتُمْ حُرُمٌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحْكُمُ مَا يُرِيْدُ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AAWFOOA BIL-U’UQOODE AUHELLAT LAKUM BAHEEMATU AL-AANA’AAME ILLAA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM GHAYRA MUHELLEAA AS-SAYDE WA ANTUM HURUMUN INNAL LAAHA YAHKOMO MAA YOREEDO.\nO’ ye who believe! Fulfil the contracts made (by you); lawful are made for you (the grass eating) quadrupeds except those which are recited unto you, not allowing the game while ye are under (the prescribed) pilgrimage restrictions, Verily, God commandeth whatever He intendeth.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُحِلُّوْا شَعَآئِرَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا الشَّهْرَ الْحَرَامَ وَلَا الْهَدْىَ وَلَا الْقَلَٓائِدَ وَلَاۤ آٰمِّيْنَ الْبَيْتَ الْحَرَامَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَرِضْوَانًا ؕ وَاِذَا حَلَلْتُمْ فَاصْطَادُوْا ؕ وَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَاٰنُ قَوْمٍ اَنْ صَدُّوْكُمْ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اَنْ تَعْتَدُوْا ۘ وَتَعَاوَنُوْا عَلَى الْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰى وَلَا تَعَاوَنُوْا عَلَى الْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(2)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TUHELLOOA SHAA’AAERA LAAHE WA LAA SHAHRA HARAAMA WA LAA AL-HADAAA WA LAA AL-QALAAAEDA WA LAA AAAAMMEENA BAYTA HARAAMA YABTAGHOONA FAZLAM MIN RABBEHIM WA RIZWAANANW WA EZAA HALALTUM FAASTAADOOA WA LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHANAANU QAWMIN AN SADDOOKUM A’NIL MASJEDIL HARAAME AN LAA WATAA’AAWANOOA A’LAL AL-BERRE WA TAQWAA WA LAA TAA’AAWANOOA A’LAL AL-AESME WAL U’UDWAANE WAT TAQUL LAAHA INNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nO ‘ ye who believe! violate not the (sanctity of) the Monuments of God, nor the sacred month nor the offering nor the symbolic garlands (wearing) nor those repairing to the Sacred House, seeking the Grace from their Lord, and (His) pleasure; and when ye are free from the (prescribed restrictions of the pilgrimage), then (ye may) hunt; and let not malice of a people, because they hindered you from the sacred Mosque, incite you to exceed the limits, and help ye (one another) in righteousness and piety, and help ye not (one another) in sin and aggression and take ye shelter in God (for). Verily, God is severe in punishment.\nحُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةُ وَالدَّمُ وَلَحْمُ الْخِنْزِيْرِ وَمَاۤ اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖ وَالْمُنْخَنِقَةُ وَالْمَوْقُوْذَةُ وَالْمُتَرَدِّيَةُ وَالنَّطِيْحَةُ وَمَاۤ اَكَلَ السَّبُعُ اِلَّا مَا ذَكَّيْتُمْ وَمَا ذُ بِحَ عَلَى النُّصُبِ وَاَنْ تَسْتَقْسِمُوْا بِالْاَزْلَامِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ فِسْقٌ ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ يَئِسَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ دِيْنِكُمْ فَلَا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَاخْشَوْنِ ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ اَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِيْنَكُمْ وَاَ تْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِىْ وَرَضِيْتُ لَكُمُ الْاِسْلَامَ دِيْنًا ؕ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ فِىْ مَخْمَصَةٍ غَيْرَ مُتَجَانِفٍ لِّاِثْمٍۙ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏‏(3)\nHURREMAT A’LAYKOMUL ARZUL MAYTAH WAALDDAMU WALAHMU KHINZEERE WA MAA OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI WAL MUNKHANEQATU WAL MAWQOOZATU WAL MUTARADDEETU WAALNNATEEHATU WA MAA AAKALA AS-SABUU’U ILLAA MAA ZAKKAYTUM WA MAA ZU BEHA A’LAL AN-NUSUBE WA TASTAQSEMOOA BIL-AAZLAAME ZAA ZAALEKUM FESQUN AL-YAWMA YAESA LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN DEENEKUM FALAA TAKHSHAWHUM WAAKHSHAWNE AL-YAWMA AAKMALTU LAKUM DEENAKUM WA TMAMTU A’LAYKUM NE’MATEE WARAZEETU LAKOMUL AL-AESLAAMA DEENAN FAMANE’ TURRA FEE MAKHMASATIN GHAYRA MUTAJAANEFIN LEAESMIN FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nForbidden unto you is the Dead (that which dieth of itself) and blood, and flesh of swine, and what hath been (slaughtered) in the name of any other than that of Allah, and the strangled, and the beaten to death, and the killed by a fall, and the gored to death by a horn, and that which the wild beasts ate, except what ye slaughter (in accordance with the prescribed law) and (also forbidden is to you) what is sacrificed on altar stones (unto idols), and that (which) ye divide by consulting arrows, Al! these is abomination; This day are despaired those who disbelieve, against your (reverting from your) religion, so ye fear them not but fear Me; This day have I perfected for you, your religion, and have completed My favour on you, and chosen for you ISLAM (to be) the Religion; But whoever is helplessly forced by hunger, not inclining to sin then Verily, God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ مَاذَاۤ اُحِلَّ لَهُمْؕ قُلْ اُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتُ ۙ وَمَا عَلَّمْتُمْ مِّنَ الْجَوَارِحِ مُكَلِّبِيْنَ تُعَلِّمُوْنَهُنَّ مِمَّا عَلَّمَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فَكُلُوْا مِمَّاۤ اَمْسَكْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(4)\nYAS-ALOONAKA MAA OHILLA LAHUM QUL OHILLA LAKOMUL AT-TAYBAATU WA MAA A’ALLAMTUM MENAL AL-JAWAAREHE MUKALLEBEENA TUA’ALLEMOONAHUNNA MIMMAA A’ALLAMAKUMU LAAHO FA-KOLOO MIMMAA AAMSAKNA A’LAYKUM WAZ KORUL KORISMA LAAHE A’LAYHE WAT TAQUL LAAHA INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThey ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) what is made lawful for them (in food) Say: “Lawful have been made for you the good things, and (as to the prey of) what ye have taught from among the hunting beasts the dog and which ye have trained them, ye teach them, even as God hath taught you, then eat ye of what they hold for you, and mention the name of Allah on the prey (while ye leave the beast to catch it), and fear God; Verily, God is swift in reckoning”.\nاَلْيَوْمَ اُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتُ ؕ وَطَعَامُ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا الْكِتٰبَ حِلٌّ لَّکُمْ وَطَعَامُكُمْ حِلٌّ لَّهُمْ وَالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ وَالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ اِذَاۤ اٰتَيْتُمُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ مُحْصِنِيْنَ غَيْرَ مُسَافِحِيْنَ وَلَا مُتَّخِذِىْۤ اَخْدَانٍؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِالْاِيْمَانِ فَقَدْ حَبِطَ عَمَلُهٗ وَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(5)\nAL-YAWMA OHILLA LAKOMUL AT-TAYBAATU WA TA-A’AMO LAZEENA OOTOO KETAABA HILLUM LLAM WATAA’AAMUKUM HILLUM LAHUM WAL MUHSANAATU MENAL MOAMENAATE WAL MUHSANAATU MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM EZAA MIMMAA OJOORAHUNNA MUHSENEENA GHAYRA MUSAAFEHEENA WA LAA MUTTAKHEZEAA AAKHDAANIN WA MAN YAKFUR BIL-EEMAANE FAQAD HABETA A’AMALUH WA HOWA FIL AAKHERATE MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nThis day have been made lawful for you (all) good things; and the food of those who have been given the Book hath been made lawful to you, and your food is lawful for them, and the chaste (ones) from the believing women, and the chaste* (ones) from those who have been given the Book before you (are lawful for you) when ye have given them their wage (dower) with chaste intention (of a lawful wedlock) nor fornicating, nor taking them for paramours in secret; and he who denieth faith, indeed, become vain all his deeds, and in the hereafter he shall be of the losers.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا قُمْتُمْ اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ فَاغْسِلُوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ وَاَيْدِيَكُمْ اِلَى الْمَرَافِقِ وَامْسَحُوْا بِرُءُوْسِكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ اِلَى الْكَعْبَيْنِ ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ جُنُبًا فَاطَّهَّرُوْا ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضَىٰۤ اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ اَوْ جَآءَ اَحَدٌ مِّنْكُمْ مِّنَ الْغَآئِطِ اَوْ لٰمَسْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوْا مَآءً فَتَيَمَّمُوْا صَعِيْدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوْا بِوُجُوْهِكُمْ وَاَيْدِيْكُمْ مِّنْهُ ؕ مَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيَجْعَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ حَرَجٍ وَّلٰكِنْ يُّرِيْدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ وَ لِيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA QUMTUM ELAL AS-SALAAWTE FAAGHSELOOA WOJOOHAKUM WA AYDEYAKUM ELAL AL-MARAAFEQE WAAMSAHOOA BERUOOSEKUM WAARJULAKUM ELAL AL-KAA’BAYNE WA KUNTUM JUNUBAN FAATTAHHAROOA WA KUNTUM MMARZAA AW A’LAA SAFARIN AW JAAA-A AHAD MINKUM MENAL AL-GHAAETE AW LAAMASTUMU NESAAA-A FALAM WA LAM MAAA-AN FATAYAMMAMOOA SAE’EEDAN TAYYEBAA FAAMSAHOOA BEWUJOOHEKUM WA AYDEEKUM MINHO MAA YOREEDO LAAHO LEEJA’ALA A’LAYKUM MIN HARAJIN LAAKIL YYUREEDU LEETAHHERAKUM WA LEETEMMA NE’MATAHU A’LAYKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nO’ ye who believe! when ye get ready unto prayers, wash ye your faces and your hands with the elbows, and wipe a part of your heads and a part of your feet to the ankles; and if ye be polluted then ye cleanse yourselves; and if ye be sick or on a journey, or cometh one of you from the privy (after answering a call of nature), or ye have touched the women, then find ye not water, then betake ye lo pure earth and wipe ye a part of your faces and a part of your hands with it; intendeth not God that He layeth on you a difficulty, but intendeth He that He purifieth you so that He may complete His favour on you, that happly ye may be grateful.\nوَاذْکُرُوْ انِعْمَةَ اللهِ عَلَیْکُمْ وَمِیْثَاقَهُ الَّذِیْ وَاثَقَکُمْ بِهۤ ۙ اِذْقُلْتُمْ سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا وَاتَّقُوا اللهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللهَ عَلِیْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(7)\nWAAZROO ANEA’MATA LAAHIR A’ALAM WAMESAAQAHU ALLAZE WAASAQAM BEH AEZQULTUM SAMEA’NAA WA ATA’NAA WAT TAQUL AL-LHA INNAL AL-LHA A’ALEMUN BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nAnd remember ye the bounties of God on you, and His covenant He hath bound you with, when ye said “We have heard (Thy Commandment) and we have obeyed (it sincerely)-,” And fear ye God; Verily, God knoweth whatever is (hidden) in your breasts (hearts).\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُوْنُوْا قَوَّا امِيْنَ لِلّٰهِ شُهَدَآءَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَاٰنُ قَوْمٍ عَلٰٓى اَ لَّا تَعْدِلُوْا ؕ اِعْدِلُوْا هُوَ اَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوٰى وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(8)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOONOO QAWA AMEENA LILLAAHE SHOHADAAA-A BIL QISTE WA LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHANAANU QAWMIN A’LAA A’ZAABAN LAA TAA’DELOOA AEA’DELOOA HOWA AQRABO LELTTAQWAA WAT TAQUL LAAHA INNAL LAAHA KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nO’ ye who believe! be always upright for God, bearing witness with justice, and let not hatred of a people incite you not to act equitably; Act ye equitably that is nearer to piety, Fear ye God; Verily God is (fully) Aware of what (all) ye do.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ۙ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(9)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nGod hath promised those who believe and do good deeds, (that there is) for them pardon and great recompense.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(10)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\nAnd (as far) those who disbelieve and belie Our signs, these are the companions of the Hell-fire.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ هَمَّ قَوْمٌ اَنْ يَّبْسُطُوْۤا اِلَيْكُمْ اَيْدِيَهُمْ فَكَفَّ اَيْدِيَهُمْ عَنْكُمْۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(11)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT KOROO NEA’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ HAMMA QAWMUN AN YYABSUTOOA ELAYKUM AYDEYAHUM FA KAFFA AYDEYAHUM A’NKUM WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nO’ ye who believe! remember ye God’s bounties on you, when a people had determined to stretch forth their hands towards you, but He withheld their hands from you; So fear God; and upon God let the faithful rely.\nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِيْثَاقَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرآءِيْلَۚ وَبَعَثْنَا مِنْهُمُ اثْنَىْ عَشَرَ نَقِيْبًا ؕ وَقَالَ اللّٰهُ اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْؕ لَئِنْ اَقَمْتُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَيْتُمُ الزَّكٰوةَ وَاٰمَنْتُمْ بِرُسُلِىْ وَعَزَّرْتُمُوْهُمْ وَاَقْرَضْتُمُ اللّٰهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا لَّاُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَلَاُدْخِلَنَّكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُۚ فَمَنْ كَفَرَ بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ مِنْكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD AAKHAZA LAAHO MEESAAQA BANEE AESRAAAEELA WABAA’ASNAA MENHUMU ASNAA A’ASHARA NAQEEBAN WA QAALA LAAHO INNEE MA-A’KUM LAIL AAQAMTUMU SALAATA WAATAYTUMU ZAKAATA WA AAMANTUM BERUSULEAA WAA’AZZARTUMOOHUM WAAQRAZTUMU LAAHA QARZAN HASANAN LLAAKAFFERANNA A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WALAADKHELANNAKUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO FAMAN KAFARA BA’DA ZAA LEKA MINKUM FAQAD ZALLA SAWAAA-AS SABEELE.\nAnd certainly did take God, a covenant from the children of Israel and We raised up from among them Twelve chieftains; and said God: “Verily, I am with you; if ye keep up prayer and pay the poor-rate and believe in My Apostles and Support them (with reverence) and lend unto God a goodly loan, I will certainly wipe out from you your sins, and I will certainly cause you to enter gardens beneath which rivers flow, but whosoever disbelieveth after this, from among you, he shall certainly have lost the right path.\nفَبِمَا نَقْضِهِمْ مِّيْثَاقَهُمْ لَعَنّٰهُمْ وَجَعَلْنَا قُلُوْبَهُمْ قٰسِيَةً ۚ يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ عَنْ مَّوَاضِعِهٖۙ وَنَسُوْا حَظًّا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖۚ وَلَا تَزَالُ تَطَّلِعُ عَلٰى خَآئِنَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْهُمْ فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاصْفَحْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nFA BEMAA NAQZEHEM MMEESAAQAHUM LAA’ANNAAHUM WA JA-A’LNAA QULOOBAHUM QAASEETAN YUHARREFOONA AL-KALEMA A’N MMAWAAZEE’EH WANASOOA HAZZAN MIMMAA ZUKKEROOA BEHI WA LAA TAZAALU TATTALEU’U A’LAA KHAAENATIN MINHUM ILLAA QALEELAA MINHUM FAAA’FU A’NHUM WAASFAH INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nBut for their breaking their covenant; We cursed them and made their hearts hard; they shift the words (of the Scripture) from their places, and have forgotten a part of what they were admonished with, and nor wilt thou cease to be informed of deceit from among them, except (from) a few of them, so forgive them and pass over them; Verily, God loveth the beneficent.\nوَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا نَصٰرٰٓى اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَهُمْ فَنَسُوْا حَظًّا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖ فَاَغْرَيْنَا بَيْنَهُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يُنَبِّئُهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA MENAN LAZEENA QAALOO INNAA NASAARAAA AKHAZNAA MEESAAQAHUM FANASOOA HAZZAN MIMMAA ZUKKEROOA BEHI FAAGHRAYNAA BAYNAHUMU AL-A’ADAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE WA SAWFA YUNABBEUHUMU LAAHO BEMAA KAANOO YASNAU’OONA.\nAnd of those (also) who say “Verily, We are Nazerenes “, We did take their covenant, but they have forgotten a portion of what they were admonished with, therefore we stirred up among them enmity and hatred (to last) till the day of Resurrection; And soon will God inform them of what they have been doing.\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمْ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا كُنْتُمْ تُخْفُوْنَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنْ كَثِيْرٍ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ نُوْرٌ وَّكِتٰبٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۙ‏(15)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE QAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUNAA YOBAYYENUL LAKUM KASEERAA MIMMAA KUNTUM TUKHFOONA MENAL KETAABE WAYAA’FOOA A’N KASEERIM QAD JAAA-AKUM MENAL LAAHE NOORUN WWAKETAABUN MOBEEN.\nO’ People of the Book! Indeed, Our Apostle, (Muhammad) had come unto you, manifesting unto you much of what ye had been concealing of the Book, and passing over much; Indeed hath come unto you from God, Light and a Manifesting Book (Qur’an).\nيَّهْدِىْ بِهِ اللّٰهُ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ رِضْوَانَهٗ سُبُلَ السَّلٰمِ وَيُخْرِجُهُمْ مِّنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ بِاِذْنِهٖ وَيَهْدِيْهِمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(16)\nYAHDEE BEHIL LAAHO MANIS TABA-A’L REZWAANAH SUBULA AS-SALAAME WA YUKHREJOHUM MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL NOORE BE-IZNEH WAYAHDEEHEM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nWhereby God guideth him who followeth His pleasure, into the ways of peace and taketh them out from darkness towards the Light by His will and guideth them to the path (that is) straight.\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَؕ قُلْ فَمَنْ يَّمْلِكُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا اِنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يُّهْلِكَ الْمَسِيْحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَاُمَّهٗ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(17)\nLAQAD KAFARA LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA HOWA AL-MASEEHU ABNU MARYAMA QUL FAMAN FAMANY MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW IN ARAADA AN YYUHLEKA AL-MASEEHA NA MARYAMAL WAAMMAH WA MAN FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A LILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nCertainly, infidels are they who say; “Verily, God, He is Messiah, son of Mary;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Who could hold anything against God, if He intendeth to destroy the Messiah son of Mary and his mother and (all) that is in the earth together? for unto God belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth and what is between them two; He createth what He willeth; Verily, God over all things hath power.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ وَالنَّصٰرٰى نَحْنُ اَبْنٰٓؤُا اللّٰهِ وَاَحِبَّآؤُهٗ ؕ قُلْ فَلِمَ يُعَذِّبُكُمْ بِذُنُوْبِكُمْؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ بَشَرٌ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقَ ؕ يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(18)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO WAN NASAARAA NAHNO AABNAAAUA LAAHE WAAHEBBAAUH QUL FALEMA YUA’AZZEBUKUM BEZUNOOBEKUM BAL ANTUM BASHARUM MIMMAYN KHALAQAL YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YO-A’ZZEBO MAN YASHAAA-O LILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA ELAYHE MASEER.\nAnd the Jews and the Christians say: “We are the sons of God and His beloved ones;” Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Why then doth He punish you for your sins? Nay, ye are but men of those He hath created; He pardoneth whom He pleaseth, and He punisheth whom He pleaseth; and unto God belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth; and what is between them (too); and unto Him is the ultimate return (of all).\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمْ عَلٰى فَتْرَةٍ مِّنَ الرُّسُلِ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا مَا جَآءَنَا مِنْۢ بَشِيْرٍ وَّلَا نَذِيْرٍ فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَشِيْرٌ وَّنَذِيْرٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(19)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE QAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUNAA YOBAYYENUL LAKUM A’LAA FATRATIN MENAL AR-RUSULE AN TAQOOLOO MAA JAAA-ANAA MIN BASHEERIN WA LAA NAZEERIN FAQAD JAAA-AKUM BASHEERUN WWANAZEERUN WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nO’ People of the Book! Indeed hath come unto you Our Apostle, (Muhammad) explaining unto you after the break in (the series of) Our apostles, lest ye say; “There came not unto us any bearer of glad tidings nor a warner; but now hath come unto you a Bearer of glad tidings and a Warner (Our Apostle Muhammad)’, And Verily, God, over all things, hath power.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ جَعَلَ فِيْكُمْ اَنْۢبِيَآءَ وَجَعَلَكُمْ مُّلُوْكًا  ۖ  وَّاٰتٰٮكُمْ مَّا لَمْ يُؤْتِ اَحَدًا مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LEQAWMEHI LE-QAWMEHI KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ JA-A’LA FEEKUM AMBEYAAA-AL WAJAA’ALAKUM MMULOOKAN WWAATAAKUM MAA LAM YUTE AHADAN MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd remember when Moses said unto his people: “O’ my people! Remember the bounties of God upon you when He raised prophets among you, and made you kings and gave you what He hath not given to anyone else (among the peoples) in the world.\nيٰقَوْمِ ادْخُلُوا الْاَرْضَ الْمُقَدَّسَةَ الَّتِىْ كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَرْتَدُّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِكُمْ فَتَنْقَلِبُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(21)\nLE-QAWMEHI ADKHULOOA ARZA AL-MUQADDASATA LATEE KATABAL LAAHO LAKUM WA LAA TARTADDOOA A’LAA AADBAAREKUM FATANQALEBOOA KHAASEREEN.\nO’ my people! enter ye the Holy Land which God hath assigned for you, and turn not on your backs, for then ye will return (as) losers.\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّ فِيْهَا قَوْمًا جَبَّارِيْنَ ۖ  وَاِنَّا لَنْ نَّدْخُلَهَا حَتّٰى يَخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا ۚ فَاِنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا فَاِنَّا دَاخِلُوْنَ‏(22)\nQAALOO MOOSAA INNAL FEEHAA QAWMAN JABBAAREENA WA INNAA LAN NNADKHULAHAA HATTAA YAKHRUJOOA MINHAA FA-IN YAKHROJOO MINHAA FAINNAA DAAKHELOONA.\nSaid they: “O’ Moses! Verily, there are in it people of might; and Verily, we will never enter it until they get out from it, and if they get out from it, Certainly, we will enter.\nقَالَ رَجُلٰنِ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمَا ادْخُلُوْا عَلَيْهِمُ الْبَابَۚ فَاِذَا دَخَلْتُمُوْهُ فَاِنَّكُمْ غٰلِبُوْنَ  ۚ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَتَوَكَّلُوْۤا اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(23)\nQAALA RAJOLAANE MENAL LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHEMAD KHOLOO A’LAYHEMUL BAABA, FA-EZAA DAKHALTOMOOHO FA-INNAKUM GHAALEBOON, WA A’LAL LAAHE FATAWAKKALOO IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nThen two men of those who feared (God), and upon whom both, God hath bestowed His) favour: “Enter ye upon them (suddenly) by the gate (of the city); for (once) ye have entered it, Verily, (ye shall see) ye are victorious, and upon God ye should rely, if ye be (true) believers.\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّا لَنْ نَّدْخُلَهَاۤ اَبَدًا مَّا دَامُوْا فِيْهَا فَاذْهَبْ اَنْتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَاتِلَاۤ اِنَّا هٰهُنَا قَاعِدُوْنَ‏(24)\nQAALOO MOOSAA INNAA LAN NNADKHULAHAA ABADAM MAA DAAMOOA FEEHAA FAAZHAB ANTA WA RABBOKA FAQAATELAA INNAA HAAHUNAA QAAE’EDOONA.\nSaid they: “O’ Moses! Verily, Never shall we enter it at all, while they remain therein, go thou and thy Lord and fight ye two Verily, we shall stay here sitting.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ لَاۤ اَمْلِكُ اِلَّا نَفْسِىْ وَاَخِىْ فَافْرُقْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE LAA AAMLEKU ILLAA NAFSEE WA AKHEE FAAFRUQ BAYNANAA WA BAYNA QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nSaid he (Moses), “O’ My Lord! No hold have I, except on myself and my Brother, so cause (Thou), a separation between us and the people (who are) rebellious.\nقَالَ فَاِنَّهَا مُحَرَّمَةٌ عَلَيْهِمْ اَرْبَعِيْنَ سَنَةً  ۚ يَتِيْهُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ فَلَا تَاْسَ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA FA INNAHAA MUHARRAMATUN A’LAYHIM ARBA-E’ENA SANATAN YATEEHOONA FIL ARZE FALAA TAASA A’LAL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nSaid He (God), “Forbidden it shall be upon them, the land for forty years; They shall wander (perplexed) in the earth; therefore, grieve not over the people (who are) rebellious.\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ ابْنَىْ اٰدَمَ بِالْحَقِّۘ اِذْ قَرَّبَا قُرْبَانًا فَتُقُبِّلَ مِنْ اَحَدِهِمَا وَلَمْ يُتَقَبَّلْ مِنَ الْاٰخَرِؕ قَالَ لَاَقْتُلَنَّكَؕ قَالَ اِنَّمَا يَتَقَبَّلُ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(27)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAA ABNAA AADAMAL BIL-HAQQE IZ QARRABAA QURBAANAN FATUQUBBELA MIN AAHADEHEMAA WA LAM YUTAQABBAL MENAL AL-AAAKHARE QAALA LAAQTULANNAKA QAALA INNAMAA YATAQABBALU LAAHO MENAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd recite unto them the story of the two sons of Adam with truth, when they both offered an offering, but it was accepted from one of them and was not accepted from the other; Said he, “I shall certainly slay thee,” (the other one) said, “Verily, Verily, God doth accept (an offering only) from those who guard (themselves against evil)\nلَئِنْۢ بَسَطْتَّ اِلَىَّ يَدَكَ لِتَقْتُلَنِىْ مَاۤ اَنَا بِبَاسِطٍ يَّدِىَ اِلَيْكَ لِاَقْتُلَكَ ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اللّٰهَ رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(28)\nLAIL BASATTTA ELAYYA YADAKA LE-KAMAA MAA ANAA BEBAASETIN YYADEAAA ELAYKA LEAAQTULAKA INNEE AKHAAFO LAAHA LAZEE HARRAMAHAA A’ALAMEEN.\nIf thou stretcheth forth thy hand towards me to slay me, I am not one to stretch forth my hand towards thee to slay thee; “Verily, I fear God, the Lord of the worlds.\nاِنِّىْۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَبُوْٓءَ بِاِثْمِىْ وَ اِثْمِكَ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِۚ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزٰٓؤُا الظّٰلِمِيْنَۚ‏‏(29)\nINNEE OREEDO AN TABOOA BEAESMEAA WA AESMEKA FA TAKOONA MIN ASHAABIL NAAR WAZAA LEKA JAZAAAUA ZAALEMEEN.\nVerily, I intend that thou beareth my sins and also thine (own) sin, and so thou wilt be of the companions of the (Hell) fire, and this is the recompense of the unjust.\nفَطَوَّعَتْ لَهٗ نَفْسُهٗ قَتْلَ اَخِيْهِ فَقَتَلَهٗ فَاَصْبَحَ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(30)\nFATAWA’AT LAHU NAFSUH QATLA AKHEEHE FAQATALAH FA ASBAHA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nSo led him his passion to slay his brother and he slew him, and he thus became one of the losers.\nفَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ غُرَابًا يَّبْحَثُ فِىْ الْاَرْضِ لِيُرِيَهٗ كَيْفَ يُوَارِىْ سَوْءَةَ اَخِيْهِؕ قَالَ يَاوَيْلَتٰٓى اَعَجَزْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِثْلَ هٰذَا الْغُرَابِ فَاُوَارِىَ سَوْءَةَ اَخِىْۚ فَاَصْبَحَ مِنَ النّٰدِمِيْنَۛ ۚ ۙ‏‏‏(31)\nFA-BA-A’SAL LAAHO GHURAABAN YYABHASU FEE ARZE LEEREEH KAYFA YOOAREAA SAWATA AAKHEEHE QAALA YAAWAYLATAAA AAA’AJAZTU AN SHAY-IWN WA MISLA HAAZAA AL-GHURAABE FAAWAAREAAA SAWATA AAKHEAA FA ASBAHA MENAL AN-NAADEMEENA.\nThen sent God, a crow digging the earth so that he might show him, how he should cover the unsightly corpse of his brother; (seeing this) Said he, “Woe unto me! Am I unable to be like this crow to cover the unsightly corpse of my brother?” So he became of the repentants.\nمِنْ اَجْلِ ذٰ لِكَ ۛ ؔ ۚ كَتَبْنَا عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ قَتَلَ نَفْسًۢا بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ اَوْ فَسَادٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَكَاَنَّمَا قَتَلَ النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَمَنْ اَحْيَاهَا فَكَاَنَّمَاۤ اَحْيَا النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُنَا بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ثُمَّ اِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فِى الْاَرْضِ لَمُسْرِفُوْنَ‏(32)\nMIN AAJLE ZAA LEKA KATABNAA A’LAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ ANNAHU MAN QATALA NAFSAN BEGHAYRIL NAFSIM AW FASAADIN FIL ARZE FAKAANNAMAA QATALA NAASA JAMEE-A’A WA MAN LAZEE FAKAANNAMAA AAHYAA NAASA JAMEE-A’A WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM ROSOLONAA BIL-BAYYENAATE SUMMA INNAL KASEERAA MINHUM BA’DA ZAA LEKA FIL ARZE LAMUSREFOONA.\nFor this reason did we prescribe unto the children of Israel that he who slayeth any one (man), without (that being for) murder, or for mischief in the land, (It shall be) as though he hath slain mankind as a whole; and he who saveth it (a human life), shall be as though he hath saved mankind as a whole; and certainly our Apostles came unto them with clear evidences and yet verily, many of them even after that certainly commit excesses in the land.\nاِنَّمَا جَزٰٓؤُا الَّذِيْنَ يُحَارِبُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَسَادًا اَنْ يُّقَتَّلُوْۤا اَوْ يُصَلَّبُوْۤا اَوْ تُقَطَّعَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَاَرْجُلُهُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ اَوْ يُنْفَوْا مِنَ الْاَرْضِؕ ذٰ لِكَ لَهُمْ خِزْىٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَ لَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ ۙ‏(33)\nINNAMAA JAZAAAUA LAZEENA YUHAAREBOONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAYASA’AWNA FIL ARZE FASAADAA AN YYUQATTALOOA AW YUSALLABOOA AW TUQATTAA’A AYDEEHIM WA ARJOLOHUM MIN KHELAAFIN AW YUNFAWA MENAL ARZ ZAA LEKA LAHUM KHIZYUN FIL DUNYAA WA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nThe recompense of those who war against God and His Apostle, and strive in the land, spreading-mischief (therein), is only that they be slain or crucified or their hands and their feet should be cut off, from the opposite sides, or be banished from the land; This, for them shall be the dis-grace in this world, and for them, in the hereafter, shall be a great torment.\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَقْدِرُوْا عَلَيْهِمْۚ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(34)\nILLAA LAZEENA TAABOO MIN QABLE AN TAQDEROO A’LAYHIM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nExcept those who repent before ye gain power over them; Know ye! that God is Oft-Pardoning, Merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَابْتَغُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ وَجَاهِدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(35)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WAB-TAGHOO ELAYHE AL-WASEELATA WAJAAHEDOOA FEE SABEELEH LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Fear God and seek ye an approach unto Him, and strive hard in His way, that ye may be successful.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ اَنَّ لَهُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لِيَفْتَدُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَا تُقُبِّلَ مِنْهُمْۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(36)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW ANNAL LAHUM MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A WWAMESLAH MA-A’HU LEEFTADOOA BEHI MIN A’ZAABIN YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAA TUQUBBELA MINHUM WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nVerily, those who disbelieve, if they had what is in the earth all together and the like of it with it, so that they ransom with it from the torment of the Day of Resurrection; (it shall) not be accepted from them and for them; there is a painful torment.\nيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنَ النَّارِ وَمَا هُمْ بِخَارِجِيْنَ مِنْهَا وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(37)\nYOREEDOONA AN YAKHROJOO MENAL NAAR WA MAA HUM BEKHAAREJEENA MINHAA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\nThey would desire to get out from the (Hell) fire, but they shall not get out (of it); and for them shall be a torment lasting.\nوَالسَّارِقُ وَالسَّارِقَةُ فَاقْطَعُوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمَا جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَسَبَا نَكَالًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(38)\nWAALSSAAREQU WAALSSAAREQATU FAAQTAU’OOA AAYDEEHUMAA JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KASABAA NAKAALAN MENAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAs for the man who stealeth and the woman who stealeth, cut ye off their (right) hands; as a recompense for what they (two) have earned; as an exemplary punishment from God; And God is Mighty, Wise.\nفَمَنْ تَابَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ظُلْمِهٖ وَاَصْلَحَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَتُوْبُ عَلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(39)\nFAMAN TAABA MIN BA’DE ZULMEH WAASLAHA FA-INNAL LAAHA YATOOBU A’LAYH INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd he who turneth (to God, repent) after his iniquity, and reformeth (himself); then, Verily, God turneth unto him (mercifully, pardons him); Verily, God is Oft-Pardoning, Merciful.\nاَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(40)\nALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ YO-A’ZZEBO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nDost not thou know that God, to Him belongeth the Dominion of the heavens and the earth; He punisheth whom He pleaseth, and pardoneth whom He pleaseth; And Verily, God over all things hath power.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرَّسُوْلُ لَا يَحْزُنْكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِى الْكُفْرِ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ ۛۚ وَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا  ۛۚ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لِلْكَذِبِ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لِقَوْمٍ اٰخَرِيْنَۙ لَمْ يَاْتُوْكَؕ يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَوَاضِعِهٖۚ يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنْ اُوْتِيْتُمْ هٰذَا فَخُذُوْهُ وَاِنْ لَّمْ تُؤْتَوْهُ فَاحْذَرُوْا ؕ وَمَنْ يُّرِدِ اللّٰهُ فِتْنَتَهٗ فَلَنْ تَمْلِكَ لَهٗ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًاؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يُرِدِ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّطَهِّرَ قُلُوْبَهُمْ ؕ لَهُمْ فِىْ الدُّنْيَا خِزْىٌ ۚۖ وَّلَهُمْ فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(41)\nYAA AYYOHAL RASOOLO LAA YAHZUNKA LAZEENA YUSAAREU’OONA FIL AL-KUFRE MENAL LAZEENA QAALOO AAMANNAA BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM WA LAM TUMEN QULOOBUHUM WA MENAN LAZEENA HAADOO SAMMAAU’OONA LIL-KAZEBE SAMMAAU’OONA LE-QAWMIN-Y AAKHEREEN LAM YAATOOKA YUHARREFOONA AL-KALEMA MIN BA’DE MAWAAZEE’EH YAQOOLOONA IN MAA OOTEETUM HAAZAA FA-KHOZOOH WA LAM TUTAWHU FAAHZAROOA WA MAN YYUREDE LAAHO FETNATAH FALAN TAMLEKA LAHU MENAL LAAHE SHAYAN OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LAM YUREDE LAAHO AN YYUTAHHERA QULOOBAHUM LAHUM FEE DUNYAA KHIZYUN WA LAHUM FEE AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\n(O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Let not those who hasten in infidelity grieve thee, of those who say “We believe” with their mouths and their hearts believe not; and of those who are Judaised (they are) listeners to (the) lie, listeners for other people (who have) not come unto thee; they distort the words from their (original) places (in the law) saying (to the people) “If ye are given this (by Muhammad) take ye, and if ye are not given this, beware! (Be aloof)’’’ and (as for him) whom God desireth to try, thou canst never prevail with God in anything; Those are they whom God willeth not that He purifieth their hearts; for them (shall be) in this world disgrace, and for them in the hereafter (shall be) a great punishment.\nسَمّٰعُوْنَ لِلْكَذِبِ اَ كّٰلُوْنَ لِلسُّحْتِؕ فَاِنْ جَآءُوْكَ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ اَوْ اَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ فَلَنْ يَّضُرُّوْكَ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاِنْ حَكَمْتَ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِيْنَ‏(42)\nSAMMAAU’OONA LIL-KAZEBE A’ZAABAN KKAALOONA LELSSUHTE FA-IN JAAOOKA FAAHKUM BAYNAHUM AW AAA’REZ A’NHUM WA TUA’REZ A’NHUM FALAN YYAZURROOKA SHAY-ANW WA HAKAMTA FAAHKUM BAYNAHUM BIL QISTE INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL AL-MUQSETEENA.\n(They are) listeners to (any) lie, devourers of the illicit gain therefore if they come unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) (thou art at liberty to) judge between them or turn aside from them; And if thou turneth aside from them, then never shall they harm thee in any way, but if thou judge, judge thou between them with equity; verily God loveth those who deal equitably.\nوَكَيْفَ يُحَكِّمُوْنَكَ وَعِنْدَهُمُ التَّوْرٰٮةُ فِيْهَا حُكْمُ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ ؕ وَمَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(43)\nWA KAYFA YUHAKKEMOONAKA WAE’ENDAHUMU AT-TAWRAATU FEEHAA HUKMU LAAHE SUMMA YATAWALLAWNA MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA WA MAA OOLAAA-EKA BIL-MOAMENEENA.\nBut how shall they make thee their Judge, while with them is the Torah wherein is (the clear) judgment of God, and yet they turn away (even) after that; and (in fact) these are not believers.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا التَّوْرٰٮةَ فِيْهَا هُدًى وَّنُوْرٌ ۚ يَحْكُمُ بِهَا النَّبِيُّوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسْلَمُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَ الرَّبَّانِيُّوْنَ وَالْاَحْبَارُ بِمَا اسْتُحْفِظُوْا مِنْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ وَكَانُوْا عَلَيْهِ شُهَدَآءَ ۚ فَلَا تَخْشَوُا النَّاسَ وَاخْشَوْنِ وَلَا تَشْتَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِىْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(44)\nINNAA ANZALNAA TAWRAATA FEEHAA HODAM WWANOORUN YAHKOMO BEHAA NABIYYOONA LAZEENA AASLAMOOA LILLAZEENA HAADOO WA AR-RABBAANEEWNA WAL AAHBAARU BEMAA ASTUHFEZOOA MIN KETAABIL LAAHE WA KAANOO A’LAYHE SHOHADAAA-A FALAA TAKHSHAWUA NAASA WAAKHSHAWNE WA LAA TASHTAROO BE-AAYAATEE SAMANAN QALEELAA WA MAN LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAAFEROON.\nVerily We sent down the Torah therein was guidance and light; with it judged (Our) apostles who submitted themselves (to Us) for those who had Judaized, and (so used to do) the divines (the Priests of the Jews - the Rabbis), and the Scholars (of divinity of the Jews) In accordance with what they were entrusted with the Book of God and they were witnesses thereof; therefore fear not the people, and fear Me, and barter not away My Signs for a small price; and whoever judgeth not by what God hath sent down, those are they that are the infidels.\nوَكَتَبْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ فِيْهَاۤ اَنَّ النَّفْسَ بِالنَّفْسِۙ وَالْعَيْنَ بِالْعَيْنِ وَالْاَنْفَ بِالْاَنْفِ وَالْاُذُنَ بِالْاُذُنِ وَالسِّنَّ بِالسِّنِّۙ وَالْجُرُوْحَ قِصَاصٌؕ فَمَنْ تَصَدَّقَ بِهٖ فَهُوَ كَفَّارَةٌ لَّهٗ ؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(45)\nWAKATABNAA A’LAYHIM FEEHAA ANNAL AN-NAFSA BEALNNAFSE WAL A’AYNA BIL-A’AYNE WAL AANFA BIL-AANFE WAL AUZUNA BIL-AUZUNE WAALSSENNA BEALSSENNE WAL JUROOHA QESAAS FAMAN TASADDAQA BEHI FAHOWA KAFFAARATUN LAHU WA MAN LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL ZAALEMOON.\nAnd We prescribed for them (therein) that life is for life, and eye for eye, and nose for nose, and ear for ear, and tooth for tooth, and for wounds (there shall be a) reprisal; but he who remitteth it (in charity), it shall be an expiation (of his sins) for him; and whoso judgeth not by what God hath sent down, these, then are the unjust.\nوَقَفَّيْنَا عَلٰٓى اٰثَارِهِمْ بِعِيْسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْاِنْجِيْلَ فِيْهِ هُدًى وَّنُوْرٌ ۙ وَّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَهُدًى وَّمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ ؕ‏(46)\nWA QAFFAYNAA A’LAA AAASAAREHEM BE-E’ESAB MARYAM MARYAMAL MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAL WA WA AATAYNAAHO AL-AENJEELA FEEHE HODAM WWANOORUN WA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAL WA WA HODANW WWAMAWE’EZATAN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd We caused to follow in their footsteps, Jesus son of Mary, confirming the law (The Torah) which was before him, and We gave him the Evangel in which was guidance and light and confirmation of what was before it of the Torah, and a guidance and an admonition for those who guard (against evil).\nوَلْيَحْكُمْ اَهْلُ الْاِنْجِيْلِ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(47)\nWALYAHKUM AAHLU INJEELE BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FEEH WA MAN LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nAnd let the people of the Evangel judge according to what God hath sent down in it; and whoever judgeth not by what God hath sent down; these then are the transgressors.\nوَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَمُهَيْمِنًا عَلَيْهِ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ عَمَّا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْحَقِّؕ لِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنَا مِنْكُمْ شِرْعَةً وَّمِنْهَاجًا ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ لِّيَبْلُوَكُمْ فِىْ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْ فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرٰتِؕ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَۙ‏(48)\nWA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KETAABA BIL-HAQQE MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAL KETAABE WAMUHAYMENAN A’LAYHE FAAHKUM BAYNAHUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABEA’ AHWAAA-AHUM A’MMAA JAAA-AKA MENAL HAQQ LEKULLIN JA-A’LNAA MINKUM SHERA’ATAN WWAMENHAAJAN WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAA’ALAKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LAAKIL LLEEBLOOKUM FEE MAA AATAAKUM MOWALLEEHAA AL-KHAYRAATE ELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’A FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nAnd We have sent down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) the Book (the Holy Qur’an) with truth, confirming what is before it of the Book and a guardian over it, therefore judge between them by what God hath sent down, and follow not their (vain) desires, diverging from what hath come unto thee, of the Truth; For every one of you We appointed a law and a (clear) way; And if God had desired, He would have made you (all) a single community but that He might try you in what He hath given (to each of) you Therefore compete ye excelling one another in goodness; Unto God is the return of you all, and then He shall declare unto you that wherein ye differed.\nوَاَنِ احْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ وَاحْذَرْهُمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنُوْكَ عَنْۢ بَعْضِ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْكَؕ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاعْلَمْ اَنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَهُمْ بِبَعْضِ ذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ لَفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA SAALEHAN AHKUM BAYNAHUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABEA’ AHWAAA-AHUM WAAHZARHUM AN YYAFTENOOKA A’N BAA’ZE MAA ANZALAL LAAHO AELAYKA FA-IN TAWALLAW FAAA’LAM ANNAMAA YOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUSEEBAHUM BE-BA’ZIL ZUNOOBEHEM WA INNA KASEERAA MENAL NAASE LAFAASEQOONA.\nAnd (God commandeth) that thou shouldst judge between them by what God hath sent down, and follow not their vain desires, and be cautious of them, lest they beguile thee from (any) part of what God hath sent unto thee; and if they turn back, then know thou that God desireth to afflict them for some of their sins; and verily, many of the people are transgressors.\nاَفَحُكْمَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ يَبْغُوْنَؕ وَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ حُكْمًا لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(50)\nAAFAHUKMA JAAHELIYYATIL YABGHOONA WA MAN AHSANO MENAL LAAHE HUKMAWN LEQAWMINY YOOQENOON.\nIs it (then that) the Judgment of (the times of pagan) ignorance they desire? And who (else) can be better than God to judge for a people of assured faith.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الْيَهُوْدَ وَالنَّصٰرٰۤى اَوْلِيَآءَ ؔۘ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّهُمْ مِّنْكُمْ فَاِنَّهٗ مِنْهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(51)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AL-YAHOODA WAN NASAARAA AAWLEEAAAA KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z WA WA MAN YYATAWALLAHUM MINKUM FA-INNAHU MENHUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nO’ ye who believe! take ye not the Jews and the Christians for friends, they are friends one of the other; and whoever taketh them for friends of you, verily, he is one of them; Verily, God guideth not an unjust people.\nفَتَرَى الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ يُّسَارِعُوْنَ فِيْهِمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ نَخْشٰٓى اَنْ تُصِيْبَنَا دَآئِرَةٌ ؕ فَعَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِالْفَتْحِ اَوْ اَمْرٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖ فَيُصْبِحُوْا عَلٰى مَاۤ اَسَرُّوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ نٰدِمِيْنَ ؕ‏(52)\nFATARAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN YYUSAAREU’OONA FEEHIM YAQOOLOONA NAKHSHAAA AN TUSEEBANAA DAAERATUN FAA’ASAA LAAHO AN YAATEYA BIL-FATHE AW AMRIN MIN I’NDEHI FAYUSBEHOOA A’LAA MAA AASARROOA FEE ANFOSEHIM NAADEMEENA.\nSo Seest thou those in whose hearts is disease hastening towards them, saying “We fear lest a reverse (of fortune) befall us;” But belike God bringeth about a victory (for thee) or (some) thing from Himself, then will they be regretting for what they hid in their selves.\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْۙ اِنَّهُمْ لَمَعَكُمْ ؕ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فَاَصْبَحُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA YAQOOLO LAZEENA AAMANOO AAHAAAULAAE LAZEENA AAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM INNAHUM LAMAA’AKUM HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FA-ASBAHOO KHAASEREEN.\nAnd then will say those who believe “Are these they who swore by God with the most forcible of their oaths that they were most surely with you?” In vain shall go all their (good) deeds, and they shall be losers.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَنْ يَّرْتَدَّ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِيْنِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَاْتِى اللّٰهُ بِقَوْمٍ يُّحِبُّهُمْ وَيُحِبُّوْنَهٗۤ ۙ اَذِلَّةٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَعِزَّةٍ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ يُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَخَافُوْنَ لَوْمَةَ لَاۤئِمٍ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ يُؤْتِيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(54)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MAN YARTADDA MINKUM A’N DEENEHI FA-SAWFA YAATEAA LAAHO BE-QAWMIN YYUHEBBUHUM WAYUHEBBOONAH AAZELLATIN A’LAL MOAMENEEN AAE’EZZATIN A’LAL KAAFEREEN YUJAAHEDOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA YAKHAAFOONA LAWMATA LAAEMIN ZAA LEKA FAZLUL LAAHE YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nO’ Ye who believe! whoever of you turneth away from his religion, soon will God bring (forward) a people, them He loveth and they love Him, lowly before the believers, mighty against the infidels, striving hard in God’s way, and they fear not the censure of any censurer; This is the grace of God, He giveth it to whomsoever He desireth, Verily, God is Ample-Giving, All-Knowing.\nاِنَّمَا وَلِيُّكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَهُمْ رَاكِعُوْنَ‏(55)\nINNAMAA WALEEKUMU LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU WAL LAZEENA AAMANUT LAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM RAAKEU’OONA.\nVerily, Verily, your guardian is (none else but) God and His Apostle (Muhammad) and those who believe, those who establish prayer and pay the poor-rate, while they be (even) bowing down (in prayer).\nوَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّ اللّٰهَ وَ رَسُوْلَهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَاِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA MAN YATAWALLA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FA-INNAL HEZBA LAAHE HOMUL GHAALEBOON.\nWhoever taketh is his guardian, God and His Apostle (Muhammad) and those who believe, verily, (he hath joined) God’s battalion; They are those that shall (always) be triumphant.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَكُمْ هُزُوًا وَّلَعِبًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَالْكُفَّارَ اَوْلِيَآءَ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(57)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA DEENAKUM HOZOWANW WWALAE’EBAN MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM WA KUFFAARA AAWLEEAAAA WAT TAQUL LAAHA IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nO’ ye who believe! take not those who hold your religion in mockery and fun, from among those who have been given the Book before you and the infidels, as guardians; Fear God, if ye be believers.\nوَ اِذَا نَادَيْتُمْ اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ اتَّخَذُوْهَا هُزُوًا وَّلَعِبًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA EZAA NAADAYTUM ELAL AS-SALAAWTE ATTAKHAZOOHAA HOZOWANW WWALAE’EBAN ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd when ye call to prayer, they make it a mockery and a sport; this because they are a people who understand not.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ هَلْ تَنْقِمُوْنَ مِنَّاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْنَا وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۙ وَاَنَّ اَكْثَرَكُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(59)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE HAL TANQEMOONA MINNAA ILLAA AN AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WA MAA UNZELA ELAYNAA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLO WA ANNAL AAKSARAKUM FAASEQOONA.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) O’ People of the Book! Do ye find fault with us (for aught) except that we believe in God and in what hath been sent down unto us and what had been sent down before, and that most of you are transgressors?\nقُلْ هَلْ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِشَرٍّ مِّنْ ذٰ لِكَ مَثُوْبَةً عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ مَنْ لَّعَنَهُ اللّٰهُ وَغَضِبَ عَلَيْهِ وَجَعَلَ مِنْهُمُ الْقِرَدَةَ وَالْخَنَازِيْرَ وَعَبَدَ الطَّاغُوْتَ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضَلُّ عَنْ سَوَآءِ السَّبِيْلِ‏(60)\nQUL HAL AUNABBEUKUM BESHARRIN MIN ZAA LEKA MASOOBATAN I’NDAL LAAHE MAN LLAA’ANAHU LAAHO WA GHAZEBAL A’LAYHE WA MENHUMU AL-QERADATA WAL KHANAAZEERA WAA’ABADA AT-TAAGHOOTA OOLAAA-EKA HOWA MMAKAANAN WWAAZALLU A’N SAWAAA-IL SABEELE.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) shall I inform you of worse than this in retribution, with God? (Worse is he) whom God hath cursed and brought (His) wrath upon (Him) and of whom (some) he trans-formed (into) apes and swine, and he who worshipped Taghut (devil); They are worse in place (rank) and far more astray from the (Right) path.\nوَاِذَا جَآءُوْكُمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَقَدْ دَّخَلُوْا بِالْكُفْرِ وَهُمْ قَدْ خَرَجُوْا بِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA EZAA JAAA-OOKUM QAALOO AAMANNAA WA QAD DDAKHALOOA BIL-KUFRE WA HUM QAD KHARAJOO BEH WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA KAANOO YAKTOMOONA.\nAnd when they come to you, (O’ Muslim!) they say, “We believe” and indeed they come in with infidelity (in their hearts) and indeed they have gone with it; and God knoweth best what they have been concealing (in their hearts).\nوَتَرٰى كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِى الْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَاَكْلِهِمُ السُّحْتَ ؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(62)\nWATARAA KASEERAA MINHUM YUSAAREU’OONA FIL AL-AESME WAL U’UDWAANE WAAKLEHEMU AS-SUHTA LABESA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThou dost see many of them vying with sin and exceeding the limits, and their eating what is foul; certainly evil is what they have been doing.\nلَوْلَا يَنْهٰٮهُمُ الرَّبَّانِيُّوْنَ وَالْاَحْبَارُ عَنْ قَوْلِهِمُ الْاِثْمَ وَاَكْلِهِمُ السُّحْتَؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(63)\nLAWLAA YANHAAHUMU AR-RABBAANEEWNA WAL AAHBAARU A’N QAWLEHEMU AL-AESMA WAAKLEHEMU AS-SUHTA LABESA MAA KAANOO YASNAU’OONA.\nWhy do not the learned men and the doctors of law prohibit them from uttering what is sinful and their eating of what is forbidden? Evil indeed is what they work.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ يَدُ اللّٰهِ مَغْلُوْلَةٌ ؕ غُلَّتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَلُعِنُوْا بِمَا قَالُوْا ۘ بَلْ يَدٰهُ مَبْسُوْطَتٰنِ ۙ يُنْفِقُ كَيْفَ يَشَآءُ ؕ وَلَيَزِيْدَنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ مَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ طُغْيَانًا وَّكُفْرًا ؕ وَاَ لْقَيْنَا بَيْنَهُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَوْقَدُوْا نَارًا لِّلْحَرْبِ اَطْفَاَهَا اللّٰهُ ۙ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَسَادًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(64)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO LAAHE LAAHE MAGHLOOLATUN GHULLAT AYDEEHIM WALUE’ENOOA BEMAA QAALOO BAL YADAAHO MABSOOTATAANE YUNFEQO KAYFA YASHAAA WALAYAZEEDANNA KASEERAA MINHUM MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA TUGHYAANAN WWAKUFRAN WA LQAYNAA BAYNAHUMU AL-A’ADAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE KULLAMAA AAWQADOOA NAARAN LLELHARBE AATFAAHAA LAAHO WAYASA’AWNA FIL ARZE FASAADAA WAL LAAHO LAA YOHIBBUL MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd the Jews say: The hand of God is tied up! shackled shall be their hands and be they accursed for what they say, nay both His hands are wide outstretched, He expends as He pleaseth; and what has been sent, down unto thee from thy Lord will certainly increase many of them in transgression and infidelity; and We have put enmity and hatred between them (to last) until the day of resurrection; Every time they kindle a fire for War, God extinguisheth it, and they strive to spread mischief on earth; And God loveth not the mischief makers.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ اَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّقَوْا لَكَفَّرْنَا عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَلَاَدْخَلْنٰهُمْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(65)\nWA LAW ANNAL AHLAL KETAABE AAMANOO AAMANOO LAKAFFARNAA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WALAADKHALNAAHUM JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nAnd if the people of the Book had believed and guarded (themselves against evil) We would certainly have blotted out their sins from them and We would have certainly admitted them into gardens of bliss.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اَقَامُوا التَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ لَاَ كَلُوْا مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِهِمْؕ مِنْهُمْ اُمَّةٌ مُّقْتَصِدَةٌ  ؕ وَكَثِيْرٌ مِّنْهُمْ سَآءَ مَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(66)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM AAQAAMOOA TAWRAATA WAL AENJEELA WA MAA UNZELA ELAYHIM MIN RABBEHIM LAA KALOOA MIN FAWQEHIM WA MIN TAHTE AARJULEHEM MINHUM UMMATUN MMUQTASEDATUN WA KASEERUM MINHUM SAAA-A MAA YA’MALOON.\nAnd if they (Jews and Christians’) had kept up the Law (the Torah’) and the Evangel (the Injeel) and that which was sent down unto them from their Lord (the Qur’an) they would certainly have the sustenance (of good things) from above them and beneath their feet; of them are a people who are moderate (acting upright); but most of them! evil is what they do!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرَّسُوْلُ بَلِّغْ مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ ؕ وَاِنْ لَّمْ تَفْعَلْ فَمَا بَلَّغْتَ رِسٰلَتَهٗ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(67)\nYAA AYYOHAL RASOOLO BALLEGH MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA WA LAM TAFA’AL FAMAA BALLAGHTA RESAALATAH WAL LAAHO YAA’SEMUKA MENAL NAASE INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ KAAFEREEN.\nConvey thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) that which hath already been sent down unto thee, and if thou conveyeth it not, then thou hath not conveyed (executed) the apostleship at all.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَسْتُمْ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ حَتّٰى تُقِيْمُوا التَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ وَلَيَزِيْدَنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ مَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ طُغْيَانًا وَّكُفْرًاۚ فَلَا تَاْسَ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(68)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE LASTUM A’LAA SHAY-IN HATTAA TUQEEMOOA TAWRAATA WAL AENJEELA WA MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM MIN RABBEKUM WALAYAZEEDANNA KASEERAA MINHUM MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA TUGHYAANAN WWAKUFRAN FALAA TAASA A’LAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nSay! “O people of the Book! Ye have no ground to stand upon, until ye stand fast by the Law and the Evangel and what hath been sent down unto you from your Lord;” and surely that which hath been sent down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) will increase many of them in transgression and infidelity; therefore grieve not for the infidel people.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَالصَّابِئُوْنَ وَالنَّصٰرٰى مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(69)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAADOO WAALSSAABEOONA WAN NASAARAA MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nSurely those who believe and those who are Jews and the Sabeans and the Christians and whoever believeth in God and the Last Day (of Judgment) and doeth good, no fear shall be upon them and nor shall they grieve.\nلَقَدْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَاَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ رُسُلًا ؕ كُلَّمَا جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ ۢ بِمَا لَا تَهْوٰٓى اَنْفُسُهُمْۙ فَرِيْقًا كَذَّبُوْا وَفَرِيْقًا يَّقْتُلُوْنَ‏(70)\nLAQAD AKHAZNAA MEESAAQA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WA ARSALNAA ELAYHIM ROSOLAN KULLAMAA JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM BEMAA LAA TAHWAA ANFOSOHUM FAREEQAM KAZZABOO WA FAREEQAN YYAQTULOONA.\nCertainly We took a covenant from the children of Israel and We sent unto them apostles; Whenever there came to them an apostle with what their souls did not like, some (of them) did they call liars and some they used to slay.\nوَحَسِبُوْۤا اَلَّا تَكُوْنَ فِتْنَةٌ فَعَمُوْا وَصَمُّوْا ثُمَّ تَابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ عَمُوْا وَصَمُّوْا كَثِيْرٌ مِّنْهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(71)\nWAHASEBOOA ALLAA TAKOONA FITNATUN FAA’AMOOA WASAMMOOA SUMMA TAABA LAAHO A’LAYHIM SUMMA A’AMOOA WASAMMOOA KASEERUM MINHUM WAL LAAHO BASEER BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nAnd they thought that there would be no affliction, so they became blinded and deafened; (and when they repented) then God turned merciful unto them yet again many of them became blinded and deafened; and surely God well-seeth what they do.\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ؕ وَقَالَ الْمَسِيْحُ يٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبَّكُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ مَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَاْوٰٮهُ النَّارُ ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ اَنْصَارٍ‏(72)\nLAQAD KAFARA LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA HOWA AL-MASEEHU ABNU MARYAMAL WA QAALA AL-MASEEHU YAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ BODUL LAAHA RABBEE WA TAQUL INNAHU MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAQAD HARRAMA LAAHO A’LAYHE JANNATA WAMAAWAAHU TAMASSANAN WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN ANSAAR.\nCertainly infidels are they who say; “Surely God, He is the Messiah, son of Mary;” and the Messiah (himself hath only) said: “O’ Children of Israel! worship ye (only) God, my Lord and your Lord, Surely whoever associateth (aught) with God, then God forbiddeth to him the garden (of bliss) and his abode (shall be) the (Hell) fire; and there shall not be for the unjust any helpers.\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ ثَالِثُ ثَلٰثَةٍ ۘ وَمَا مِنْ اِلٰهٍ اِلَّاۤ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ  ؕ وَاِنْ لَّمْ يَنْتَهُوْا عَمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ لَيَمَسَّنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(73)\nLAQAD KAFARA LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA SAALESU SALAASATIN WA MAA MIN ELAAHIN ILLAA ELAAHUN WAAHED WA LAM YANTAHOOA A’MMAA YAQOOLOONA LAYAMASSANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nSurely, they disbelieve who say; “Surely God is the third of the three,” and there is no God but the One God; and if they desist not from what they say, a grievous torment shall meet those who disbelieve.\nاَفَلَا يَتُوْبُوْنَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَهٗؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(74)\nAFALAA YATOOBOONA ELAL LAAHE WAYASTAGHFEROONAH WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nWill they not then turn to God and ask pardon of Him? Verily God is Oft-Pardoning Merciful.\nمَا الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اِلَّا رَسُوْلٌ ۚ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُؕ وَاُمُّهٗ صِدِّيْقَةٌ  ؕ كَانَا يَاْكُلٰنِ الطَّعَامَؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُبَيِّنُ لَهُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ ثُمَّ انْظُرْ اَ نّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(75)\nMAA AL-MASEEHU ABNU MARYAMAL ILLAA RASOOLUM QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHE AR-RUSULU WAAMMUH SEDDEEQATUN KAANAA YAAKULAANE AT-TAA’AAMA AUNZUR KAYFA NUBAYNU LAHOMUL AAYAATE SUMMA ANZUR A’ZAABAN NNAA YOAFEKOON.\nThe Messiah, son of Mary, is but an apostle; indeed apostles before him have passed away; and his mother was a Truthful Lady; (like other men and women) they both used to eat food; Behold! How clear We make for them the signs, and yet behold (how) they are turned away (from the right path).\nقُلْ اَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(76)\nQUL A’ZAABAN TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAMLEKU LAKUM BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM WAL LAAHO HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSay, (O’ Our Apostle Muham-mad) (unto them) “Do ye worship besides God that which doth not own for you any harm, (or) any profit? And God He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا تَغْلُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَ قَوْمٍ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَاَضَلُّوْا كَثِيْرًا وَّضَلُّوْا عَنْ سَوَآءِ السَّبِيْلِ‏(77)\nQUL YAA AHLA KETAABE LAA TAGHLOOA FEE DEENEKUM GHAYRA HAQQE WA LAA TATTABE-O’O AAHWAAA QAWMIN QAD ZALLOOA MIN QABLO WAAZALLOOA KASEERAA WWAZALLOOA A’N SAWAAA-IL SABEELE.\nSay! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) “O’ People of the Book! exceed not the bounds of your religion, and follow not the vain desires of the people who had gone astray aforetime and led many astray and went astray away from the right path.\nلُعِنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ عَلٰى لِسَانِ دَاوٗدَ وَعِيْسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِمَا عَصَوْا وَّكَانُوْا يَعْتَدُوْنَ‏(78)\nLUE’ENA LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ A’LAA LESAANE DAAWOODA WA E’ESABNE MARYAM MARYAMAL ZAA LEKA BEMAA A’ASAWA WWAKAANOOA YA’TADOON.\nCursed were those who believed not, from among the children of Israel, by the tongue of David and Jesus, son of Mary; this because they disobeyed and used to exceed the limits.\nكَانُوْا لَا يَتَنَاهَوْنَ عَنْ مُّنْكَرٍ فَعَلُوْهُ ؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(79)\nKAANOO LAA YATANAAHAWNA A’N MMUNKARIN FAA’ALOOHU LABESA MAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nThey used not to forbid each other the hateful things which they wrought; Surely how evil was that which they were doing.\nتَرٰى كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتَوَلَّوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْاؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا قَدَّمَتْ لَهُمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ اَنْ سَخِطَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَفِى الْعَذَابِ هُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(80)\nTARAA KASEERAA MINHUM YATAWALLAWNA LAZEENA KAFAROOA LABESA MAA QADDAMAT LAHUM ANFOSOHUM AN SAKHETA LAAHO A’LAYHIM WA A’ZAABE HUM KHAALEDOON.\nThou will see many of them befriending those who disbelieve; surely evil is that which their selves have sent before for them, for God’s wrath is on them, and in torment shall they abide.\nوَلَوْ كَانُوْا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالنَّبِىِّ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مَا اتَّخَذُوْهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ وَلٰكِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(81)\nWA LAW KAANOO YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA NESAAA-AN WA MAA UNZELA ELAYHE MAA ATTAKHAZOOHUM AAWLEEAAAA LAAKINNAL KASEERAA MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nAnd had they believed in God and the Apostle and what was sent down unto him, they would not have taken them for friends, but most of them are evil-doers.\nلَتَجِدَنَّ اَشَدَّ النَّاسِ عَدَاوَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الْيَهُوْدَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا ۚ وَلَتَجِدَنَّ اَ قْرَبَهُمْ مَّوَدَّةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا نَصٰرٰى ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ مِنْهُمْ قِسِّيْسِيْنَ وَرُهْبَانًا وَّاَنَّهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(82)\nLATAJEDANNA ASHADDA NAASE A’ADAAWATAN LIL-LAZEENA AAMANUT AL-YAHOODA WAL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO WALATAJEDANNA A’ZAABAN QRABAHUM BAYNAKUM LIL-LAZEENA AAMANUT LAZEENA QAALOO INNAA AW ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL MINHUM QESSEESEENA WARUHBAANAN WWAANNAHUM LAA YASTAKBEROONA.\nCertainly, thou wilt find the most violent of people in enmity for those who believe, (to be) the Jews and those who are polytheists; and thou wilt certainly find the nearest in friendship to those who believe (to be) those who say; “We are Christians;” This because there among them are priests and monks and because they are not elated with pride.\nوَاِذَا سَمِعُوْا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ تَرٰٓى اَعْيُنَهُمْ تَفِيْضُ مِنَ الدَّمْعِ مِمَّا عَرَفُوْا مِنَ الْحَقِّ‌ۚ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاكْتُبْنَا مَعَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(83)\nWA EZAA SAMEO’O MAA UNZELA ELAL RASOOLE TARAAA AAA’YUNAHUM TAFEEZU MENAL AD-DAME’E MIMMAA A’RAFOO MENAL HAQQE YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAMANNAA FAAKTUBNAA LAAHA SHAAHEDEEN.\nAnd when they hear (the Holy Qur’an) what hath been sent down to (Our) Apostle (Muhammad) thou wilt see their eyes overflowing with tears on account of what they recognise of the truth; say they: “O’ Our Lord! We believe, so write us down with the witnesses (of the truth).\nوَمَا لَنَا لَا نُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ الْحَقِّۙ وَنَطْمَعُ اَنْ يُّدْخِلَنَا رَبُّنَا مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(84)\nWA MAA LANAA LAA NOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WA MAA JAAA-ANAA MENAL HAQQE WANATMAU’U AN YYUDKHELANAA RABBONAA LAAHA QAWMIL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd what reasons have we that we should not believe in God and in the truth that hath come unto us while we earnestly crave that Our Lord should admit us (to heaven) with the righteous ones.\nفَاَثَابَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِمَا قَالُوْا جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(85)\nFAASAABAHUMU LAAHO BEMAA QAALOO JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAZAA LEKA JAZAAA-O MOHSENEEN.\nTherefore, God rewarded them for what they said, with gardens neath which rivers flow, (for them) to abide therein; And this (is) the recompense of the righteous ones.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(86)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\nAnd (as for) those who disbelieve and belie our signs, these shall be the inmates of flaming (Hell) fire.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُحَرِّمُوْا طَيِّبٰتِ مَاۤ اَحَلَّ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَعْتَدُوْا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(87)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TUHARREMOOA TAYYEBAATE MAA AAHALLA LAAHO LAKUM WA LAA LAA INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MO’TADEEN.\nO’ ye who believe! Forbid not (to yourselves) the good things that God hath made lawful for you and do not transgress the limits; Verily God loveth not the transgressors\nوَكُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ حَلٰلًا طَيِّبًا‌ وَّ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْتُمْ بِهٖ مُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO HALAALAN TAYYEBAA WA TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE ANTUM BEHI MOAMENOON.\nAnd eat ye of what God hath given you (for food) that which is lawful and wholesome, and fear God in whom ye believe.\nلَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِىْۤ اَيْمَانِكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ يُّؤَاخِذُكُمْ بِمَا عَقَّدْتُّمُ الْاَيْمَانَ‌ ۚ فَكَفَّارَتُهٗۤ اِطْعَامُ عَشَرَةِ مَسٰكِيْنَ مِنْ اَوْسَطِ مَا تُطْعِمُوْنَ اَهْلِيْكُمْ اَوْ كِسْوَتُهُمْ اَوْ تَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَيَّامٍ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ كَفَّارَةُ اَيْمَانِكُمْ اِذَا حَلَفْتُمْ‌ ؕ وَاحْفَظُوْۤا اَيْمَانَكُمْ‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(89)\nLAA YO-AAKHEZOKOMUL LAAHO BIL-LAGHWE FEE AYMAANEKUM WA WA LAAKIL YO-AAKHEZOKUM BEMAA A’AQQADTTUMU AL-AAYMAANA FAKAFFAARATUH AETA’AAMU A’ASHARATE MASAAKEENA MIN AAWSATE MAA TUTE’EMOONA AAHLEEKUM AW KESWATUHUM AW TAHREERU RAQABATIN FAMAN LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SALAASATE AYYAAMIN ZAA LEKA KAFFAARATU AYMAANEKUM WA EZAA HALAFTUM WAAHFAZOOA AAYMAANAKUM KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AAYAATEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nGod doth not call you to account for what is vain in your oaths, but He calleth you to account for the making of deliberate oaths; so its expiation is the feeding of ten poor men out of the moderate food you feed your families with, or their clothing or the freeing of a slave; but whosoever findeth not means (to do any of these) then (for him) fasting for three days; this is the expiation of your oaths when ye swear; Keep then your oaths; Thus doth God maketh clear to you His signs that ye may be grateful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْاَنْصَابُ وَالْاَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطٰنِ فَاجْتَنِبُوْهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(90)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAMAA AL-KHAMRU WAL MAYSERU WAL AANSAABU WAL AAZLAAMU REJSUN MIN MIN SHAYTAANE FAAJTANEBOOHU LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Intoxicants and games of chance (dedication of) stones (i.e. idols) and (divination by) arrows, are only an abomination of Satan’s handiwork, so be ye away from it so that ye may be successful.\nاِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَنْ يُّوْقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ فِى الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلٰوةِ‌ ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّنْتَهُوْنَ‏(91)\nINNAMAA YOREEDO SHAYTAANO AN YYOOQEA’A BAYNAKOMUL AL-A’ADAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA FIL KHAMRE WAL MAYSERE WAYASUDDAKUM A’N ELAA LAAHE WA A’NIL AS-SALAAWTE FA HAL ANTUM MMUNTAHOONA.\nThe Satan only desireth to cause enmity and hatred in your midst through intoxicants and gambling and keep you away from remembering God and from prayer; will ye then abstain (from them).\nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَاحْذَرُوْا‌ ۚ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا عَلٰى رَسُوْلِنَا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(92)\nWAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R WAAHZAROOA FA-IN TAWALLAYTUM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA A’LAA RASOOLENAA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd obey God, and obey the Apostle, and be ye on your guard, but if ye turn back, know ye then, that Our Apostle (Muhammad) is bound only to deliver a clear announcement (on Our behalf).\nلَيْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جُنَاحٌ فِيْمَا طَعِمُوْۤا اِذَا مَا اتَّقَوا وَّاٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ثُمَّ اتَّقَوا وَّاٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ اتَّقَوا وَّاَحْسَنُوْا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(93)\nLAYSA A’LAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JONAAHUN FEEMAA TAE’EMOOA EZAA MAA ATTAQAWA WWAAMANOOA WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SUMMA ATTAQAWA WWAAMANOOA SUMMA ATTAQAWA WWAAHSANOOA WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nOn those who believe and do good, is no blame for what they ate, (before) when they did guard themselves and did believe, and did good, still (more) they guard themselves and believe (more strongly), still (furthermore) they guard themselves and do (greater) good; and God loveth the doers of good.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَيَبْلُوَنَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِشَىْءٍ مِّنَ الصَّيْدِ تَنَالُهٗۤ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَ رِمَاحُكُمْ لِيَعْلَمَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّخَافُهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ‌ ۚ فَمَنِ اعْتَدٰى بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فَلَهٗ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(94)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAYABLOONNAKUMU LAAHO BE-SHAY-IM MENAL AS-SAYDE TANAALUH AYDEEKUM WA REMAAHUKUM LEEA’LAMA LAAHO MAN YYAKHAAFUH BIL-GHAYBE FAMANE’ TADAA BA’DA ZAA LEKA FALAHU A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nO’ Ye who believe! God will surely try you with something about the game which your hands can reach and your lances, that God might know (prove) who feareth Him unseen; and whoever exceedeth (the limits) thereafter, for him shall be a painful chastisement.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَقْتُلُوا الصَّيْدَ وَاَنْتُمْ حُرُمٌ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ قَتَلَهٗ مِنْكُمْ مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَآءٌ مِّثْلُ مَا قَتَلَ مِنَ النَّعَمِ يَحْكُمُ بِهٖ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِّنْكُمْ هَدْيًاۢ بٰلِغَ الْكَعْبَةِ اَوْ كَفَّارَةٌ طَعَامُ مَسٰكِيْنَ اَوْ عَدْلُ ذٰ لِكَ صِيَامًا لِّيَذُوْقَ وَبَالَ اَمْرِهٖ‌ ؕ عَفَا اللّٰهُ عَمَّا سَلَفَ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ عَادَ فَيَنْتَقِمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْهُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ ذُو انْتِقَامٍ‏(95)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAQTULOOA AS-SAYDA WA ANTUM HURUMUN WA MAN QATALAH MINKUM MMUTAA’AMMEDAN FAJAZAAUN MMESLU MAA QATALA MENAL AN-NAA’AME YAHKOMO BEHI ZAWAA ZAWAY MINKUM HADYAN BAALEGHA AL-KAA’BATE AW KAFFAARATUN TA-A’AMO MASAAKEENA AW A’ADLU ZAA LEKA SEEAMAN LLEEZOOQA WA BAALA AMREHI A’AFAA LAAHO A’MMAA SALAFA WA MAN A’ADA FAYANTAQEMU LAAHO MINHO WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN ZUL ANTEQAAMIN.\nO’ ye who believe! kill ye not (any) game while ye are in the pilgrim garb; and whoever among you killeth it intentionally, the compensation (of it) is the like of what he killed from the cattle, as adjudged by two just men from among you, as an offering to be brought to the Ka’ba, or the expiation (of it) is the feeding of the poor or the equivalent of it in fasting, that he may taste the heinousness of his deed; God hath pardoned what is gone by; and whoever returneth (to it); then will God exact penalty from him, and God is Mighty, Lord of Retribution.\nاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَحْرِ وَطَعَامُهٗ مَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِلسَّيَّارَةِ‌ ۚ وَحُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَرِّ مَا دُمْتُمْ حُرُمًا‌ ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(96)\nOHILLA LAKUM SAYDU BAHRE WATAA’AAMUH MATAA-A’M LAKUM WALELSSAYARATE WAHURREMA A’LAYKUM SAYDU BARRE MAA DUMTUM HURUMAN WAT TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nAllowed unto you is the game of the sea and eating thereof a provision for you and for the travellers; and forbidden unto you is the game of the land so long as ye are in the pilgrim garb; and fear ye God unto Whom ye shall be gathered.\nجَعَلَ اللّٰهُ الْكَعْبَةَ الْبَيْتَ الْحَرَامَ قِيٰمًا لِّلنَّاسِ وَالشَّهْرَ الْحَرَامَ وَالْهَدْىَ وَالْقَلَاۤئِدَ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِتَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(97)\nJA-A’LA LAAHO AL-KAA’BATA BAYTA HARAAMA QEEMAN LIN-NAASE WA SHAHRA HARAAMA WAL HADYA WAL QALAAEDA ZAA LEKA LE-TA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA ANNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nGod hath made the Ka’ba, the Sacred House, a Sanctuary (place of stay in peace) for mankind, and the Sacred Month and the Offerings and the (animals with the) garlands, this is that ye may know that God knoweth whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, and that God is the Knower of all things.\nاِعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ ؕ‏(98)\nAEA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB WA ANNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nKnow ye! that God is severe in punishing (evil) and that God is Oft-Forgiving, Merciful.\nمَا عَلَى الرَّسُوْلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُوْنَ وَمَا تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(99)\nMAA A’LAL RASOOLE ILLAA BALAAGHUL WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TUBDOONA WA MAA TAKTOMOON.\nNothing (incumbent) is upon the Apostle but to deliver (the Message ); and God knoweth what ye reveal and what ye conceal.\nقُلْ لَّا يَسْتَوِى الْخَبِيْثُ وَالطَّيِّبُ وَلَوْ اَعْجَبَكَ كَثْرَةُ الْخَبِيْثِ‌ ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ يٰۤاُولِى الْاَ لْبَابِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(100)\nQUL LAA YASTAWEAA AL-KHABEESU WAALTTAYBU WA LAW A-A’JABAKA KASRATU AL-KHABEESE FA TAQUL LAAHA YAA AL-AA LBAABE LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nSay! (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) equal are not the bad and the good though the abundance of the bad may enchant thee; so then fear ye God, O’ ye of understanding that ye may be successful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَسْئَلُوْا عَنْ اَشْيَآءَ اِنْ تُبْدَ لَكُمْ تَسُؤْكُمْ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَسْئَلُوْا عَنْهَا حِيْنَ يُنَزَّلُ الْقُرْاٰنُ تُبْدَ لَكُمْ ؕ عَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْهَا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(101)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAS-ALOO A’N AASHYAAA IN TUBDA LAKUM TASUKUM WA TAS-ALOO A’NHAA HEENA YUNAZZALU QUR-AANO TUBDA LAKUM A’AFAA LAAHO A’NHAA WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR HALEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! ask ye not about things which if declared unto you will (only) pain you; and if ye question about them while the Qur’an is being revealed, they shall be declared unto you (but it shall annoy you), God pardoneth as to these matters; for God is Oft-Forgiving, Forbearing.\nقَدْ سَاَ لَهَا قَوْمٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكُمْ ثُمَّ اَصْبَحُوْا بِهَا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nQAD HAQ LAHAA QAWMUN MIN QABLEKUM SUMMA AASBAHOOA BEHAA KAAFEREEN.\nSurely the people before you did ask such questions and then became disbelievers therein.\nمَا جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَحِيْرَةٍ وَّلَا سَآئِبَةٍ وَّلَا وَصِيْلَةٍ وَّلَا حَامٍ‌ ۙ وَّلٰكِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ‌ ؕ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(103)\nMAA JA-A’LA LAAHO MIN BAHEERATIN WA LAA SAAEBATIN WA LAA WASEELATIN WA LAA HAAMIN WA LAAKINNA LAZEENA KAFAROO YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA WA AKSAROHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\nGod hath not ordained (the making of) a ‘Bahirah’, or a ‘Saibah’ or a ‘Wasilah’ or ‘Hami’ but those who disbelieve, fabricate a lie against God; and most of them do not understand.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَاِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ قَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا مَا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا‌ ؕ اَوَلَوْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(104)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM TA-A’ALAW ELAA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA ELAL RASOOLE QAALOO HASBUNAA MAA WAJADNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA LAW KAANA AA-BAAA-OHUM LAA YA’LAMOON SHAY-ANW WA LAA YAHTADOON.\nAnd when it is said unto them, “Come unto what God hath sent ye down unto the Apostle,” say they, “Sufficient for us is what we found our fathers upon;” What? even if their fathers knew nothing and were not (rightly) guided.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ۚ لَا يَضُرُّكُمْ مَّنْ ضَلَّ اِذَا اهْتَدَيْتُمْ‌ ؕ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(105)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO A’LAYKUM ANFOSAKUM LAA YAZURRUKUM MAN ZALLA EZAA AHTADAYTUM ELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’A FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nO’ ye who believe! On ye resteth the care of your selves, he who strayeth, cannot hurt you, when ye follow the (right) guidance, to God is the return of you all, then He shall declare unto you that which ye used to do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا شَهَادَةُ بَيْنِكُمْ اِذَا حَضَرَ اَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ حِيْنَ الْوَصِيَّةِ اثْنٰنِ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِّنْكُمْ اَوْ اٰخَرَانِ مِنْ غَيْرِكُمْ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ ضَرَبْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاَصَابَتْكُمْ مُّصِيْبَةُ الْمَوْتِ‌ ؕ تَحْبِسُوْنَهُمَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الصَّلٰوةِ فَيُقْسِمٰنِ بِاللّٰهِ اِنِ ارْتَبْتُمْ لَا نَشْتَرِىْ بِهٖ ثَمَنًا وَّلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبٰى‌ ۙ وَلَا نَكْتُمُ شَهَادَةَ ۙ اللّٰهِ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الْاٰثِمِيْنَ‏(106)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SHAHAADATU BAYNAKUM EZAA HAZARA AHADAKOMUL MAWTO HEENA AL-WASEETE ASNAANE ZAWAA ZAWAY MINKUM AW AAAKHARAANE MIN GHAYREKUM IN ANTUM ZARABTUM FIL ARZE FAASAABATKUM MMUSEEBATU MAWT TAHBESOONAHUMAA MIN BA’DE AS-SALAAWTE FAYUQSEMAANE BIL-LAAHE ENIS TABTUM LAA NASHTAREAA BEHI SAMANAN WA LAW KAANA ZAL QURBAA WA LAA NAKTUMU SHAHAADATA LAAHE INNAA EZAL LAMENAZ AL-AAASEMEENA.\nO’ ye who believe! call to witness between you when death presenteth itself unto one of you, when making a Bequest, two just persons from among you or two others from other than you, if ye be travelling in the land and the affliction of death aftlicteth you; detain the two (witnesses) after the prayer; then if ye doubt (them), they shall both swear by God (saying) “We will not take for it a price though he be a kinsman, and we will not hide the testimony of God (for them), certainly we should be among the sinners.\nفَاِنْ عُثِرَ عَلٰٓى اَنَّهُمَا اسْتَحَقَّاۤ اِثْمًا فَاٰخَرٰنِ يَقُوْمٰنِ مَقَامَهُمَا مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَحَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَوْلَيٰنِ فَيُقْسِمٰنِ بِاللّٰهِ لَشَهَادَتُنَاۤ اَحَقُّ مِنْ شَهَادَتِهِمَا وَ مَا اعْتَدَيْنَاۤ‌ ‌ۖ  اِنَّاۤ‌ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(107)\nFA-IN U’USERA A’LAA AANNAHUMAA ASTAHAQQAA ISMAN FAAKHARAANE YAQOOMAANE MAQAAMAHUMAA MENAL LAZEENA ASTAHAQQA A’LAYHEMUL AL-AAWLAYNE FAYUQSEMAANE BIL-LAAHE LASHAHAADATUNAA AHAQQO MIN SHAHAADATEHEMAA WA MAA AA’TADAYNAA INNAA EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen if it gets known that they both have been guilty of a sin (of Perjury), then two others shall stand up in their place from among those who have a claim against them, the two nearest of kin, so they two should swear by God: “certainly our testimony is truer than the testimony of those two, and we have not exceeded the limits, for then most surely we should be of the unjust.\nذٰ لِكَ اَدْنٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتُوْا بِالشَّهَادَةِ عَلٰى وَجْهِهَاۤ اَوْ يَخَافُوْۤا اَنْ تُرَدَّ اَيْمَانٌۢ بَعْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ‌ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاسْمَعُوْا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(108)\nZAA LEKA TAQARRA AN YYAATOOA BEALSSHAHAADATE A’LAA WAJHEHAA AW YAKHAAFOOA AN TURADDA AAYMAANUN BA’DA AAYMAANEHEM WAT TAQUL LAAHA WAS MA-O’O WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nThis is more proper that they give the evidence in proper manner or fear they that other oaths be given after their oaths (and they are put to shame), And fear ye God and listen; and God guideth not the transgressing people.\nيَوْمَ يَجْمَعُ اللّٰهُ الرُّسُلَ فَيَقُوْلُ مَاذَاۤ اُجِبْتُمْ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا لَا عِلْمَ لَنَا ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(109)\nYAWMA YAJMAU’U LAAHO AR-RUSULA FAYAQOOLO MAA AUJEBTUM QAALOO LAA I’LMAL LANAA INNAKA ANTA A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\n(Beware!) On the Day (of Judgment) will assemble God all the apostles and then say (asking them) “What response were ye given (to your guidance, from your people)?” They shall say (in reply) “We have no knowledge, verily Thou art the All-Knowing of the unseen.\n‌اِذْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ اذْكُرْ نِعْمَتِىْ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى وَالِدَتِكَ‌ ۘ اِذْ اَيَّدتُّكَ بِرُوْحِ الْقُدُسِ تُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِىْ الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلًا ‌ ۚوَاِذْ عَلَّمْتُكَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَالتَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ تَخْلُقُ مِنَ الطِّيْنِ كَهَيْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ بِاِذْنِىْ فَتَنْفُخُ فِيْهَا فَتَكُوْنُ طَيْرًۢا بِاِذْنِىْ‌ وَ تُبْرِئُ الْاَكْمَهَ وَالْاَبْرَصَ بِاِذْنِىْ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ تُخْرِجُ الْمَوْتٰى بِاِذْنِىْ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ كَفَفْتُ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ عَنْكَ اِذْ جِئْتَهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(110)\nIZ QAALA LAAHO YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL AZKUR NE’MATEE A’LAYKA WA A’LAA WAALEDATEKA IZ AAYDTTUKA BE-ROOHIL AL-QUDUSE TUKALLEMU NAASA FEE AL-MAHDE WAKAHLAN WA IZ A’ALLAMTUKA KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA TAWRAATA WAL AENJEELA WA IZ TAKHLUQU MENAL TEENE KAHAYATE TAYRE BEAEZNEAA FATANFUKHU FEEHAA FA TAKOONO TAYRAN BEAEZNEAA WA TUBREU AL-AAKMAHA WAL AABRASA BEAEZNEAA WA IZ TUKHREJU MAWTAA BEAEZNEAA WA IZ KAFAFTU BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ A’NKAL IZ JEATAHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAQAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nWhen God shall say: “O’ Jesus, son of Mary! Remember my favour on thee and on thy Mother, when I strengthened thee with the Holy Spirit, that thou didst speak to the people (when still a babe) in the cradle and when grown up, and when I taught thee the Book, and the Wisdom and the Torah and the Evangel, and when thou didst make of clay like the figure of a bird, by My leave and then didst breathe into it and it became a bird by My leave and didst heal the (born) blind and the lepers by My leave; and when thou didst bring forth the dead ( from their graves) by My leave; and when I did withhold the children of Israel from (hurting) thee when thou hadst come to them with clear signs (miracles) but then those who disbelieved among them said, “this is nothing but clear sorcery.\nوَ اِذْ اَوْحَيْتُ اِلَى الْحَوَارِيّٖنَ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِىْ وَبِرَسُوْلِىْ‌ۚ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَاشْهَدْ بِاَنَّنَا مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(111)\nWA IZ AAWHAYTU ELAL AL-HAWAAREENA AN AAMENOO BEE WABERASOOLEAA QAALOO AAMANNAA WAASHHAD BEAANNANAA MUSLEMOON.\nAnd when I, revealed unto the disciples, “Believe in Me and Mine Apostle (Jesus)” said they, “We believe, and bear Thou witness that we are Muslims (those who submit ourselves to God).\nاِذْ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّوْنَ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ هَلْ يَسْتَطِيْعُ رَبُّكَ اَنْ يُّنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا مَآئِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ‌ ؕ قَالَ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nIZ QAALA AL-HAWAAREEWNA YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL HAL ZA-E’EFAN RABBOKA AN YONAZZELAL A’LAYNAA MAAEDATAN MENAL SAMAAA-E QAALA TAQUL LAAHA IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nAnd (recollect) when said the Disciples “O’ Jesus, son of Mary! “Is thy Lord able that He sendeth down unto us table furnished with food from heaven?” said (Jesus) “Fear ye God! if ye be (true) believers (in Him)\nقَالُوْا نُرِيْدُ اَنْ نَّاْكُلَ مِنْهَا وَتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوْبُنَا وَنَعْلَمَ اَنْ قَدْ صَدَقْتَنَا وَنَكُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(113)\nQAALOO NOREEDO AN NNAAKULA MINHAA WATATMAENNA QOLOOBONAA WANAA’LAMA AN QAD SADAQTANAA WA NAKOONA A’LAYHAA MENAL SHAAHEDEEN.\nSaid they, “We desire to eat from it and that our hearts be satisfied and that we may know that thou hast indeed spoken the truth to us and we may be of the witnesses upon it.\nقَالَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّنَاۤ اَنْزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مَآئِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ تَكُوْنُ لَنَا عِيْدًا لِّاَوَّلِنَا وَاٰخِرِنَا وَاٰيَةً مِّنْكَ‌ۚ وَارْزُقْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL AL-LAAHUMMA RABBANAA AANZEL A’LAYNAA MAAEDATAN MENAL SAMAAA-E TAKOONO LANAA E’EEDAN LEAAWLENAA WAAKHERENAA WA AAYATAL MINKA WAARZUQNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nSaid Jesus, son of Mary, “O’ God! Our Lord! send down unto us from heaven a table set with food that it may be for us a recurring happiness, to the first of us and the last of us, and a sign from Thee; and provide us (with our) sustenance and Thou art the Best of the Sustainers.\nقَالَ اللّٰهُ اِنِّىْ مُنَزِّلُهَا عَلَيْكُمْ‌ۚ فَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بَعْدُ مِنْكُمْ فَاِنِّىْۤ اُعَذِّبُهٗ عَذَابًا لَّاۤ اُعَذِّبُهٗۤ اَحَدًا مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(115)\nQAALA LAAHO INNEE MUNAZZELUHAA A’LAYKUM FAMAN YAKFUR BA’DO MINKUM FA-INNEE AUA’AZZEBUH A’ZAABAN LAA AUA’AZZEBUH AHADAN MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nSaid God, “Verily I will send it down unto you, but whoever shall disbelieve thereafter among you, surely will I chastise him with a chastisement, which I will not chastise anyone in the worlds, with (the like of it).\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ ءَاَنْتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُوْنِىْ وَاُمِّىَ اِلٰهَيْنِ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ قَالَ سُبْحٰنَكَ مَا يَكُوْنُ لِىْۤ اَنْ اَقُوْلَ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِحَقٍّ‌ؕؔ اِنْ كُنْتُ قُلْتُهٗ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهٗ‌ؕ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِىْ نَفْسِىْ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ مَا فِىْ نَفْسِكَ‌ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(116)\nWA IZ QAALA LAAHO YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL AANTA QULTA LIN-NAASE ATTAKHEZOONEAA WAAMMEAAA AELAAHAYNE MIN DOONIL LAAH QAALA SUBHAANAKA MAA LAHUL LEE AN AAQOOLA MAA LAYSA LEE BEHAQQIN IN KUNTO QULTUH FAQAD A’ALEMTAH TAA’LAMU MAA FEE NAFSEE WA LAA A-A’LAMO MAA FEE NAFSEKA INNAKA ANTA A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\nAnd when God will say (asking) “O’ Jesus son of Mary! didst thou say to the people, take me and my mother two gods beside God?” he will say (in reply) “Glory be to Thee, it was not for me to say that which I had no right to say; If I had said it Thou wouldst have indeed known it; Thou knowest whatever is in myself and I know not what is in Thine Self; Verily Thou art the Great Knower of all the unseen.\nمَا قُلْتُ لَهُمْ اِلَّا مَاۤ اَمَرْتَنِىْ بِهٖۤ اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبَّكُمْ‌ۚ وَكُنْتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيْدًا مَّا دُمْتُ فِيْهِمْ‌ۚ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِىْ كُنْتَ اَنْتَ الرَّقِيْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ وَاَنْتَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(117)\nMAA QULTU LAHUM ILLAA MAA AAMARTANEAA BEHI SAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA RABBEE WA TAQUL WA KUNTO A’LAYHIM SHAHEEDAA MAA DUMTU FEEHIM FALAMMAA TAWAFFAYTANEAA KUNTA ANTA AR-RAQEEBA WA WA ANTA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nI did not say to them aught except what Thou didst command me with; that worship God my Lord and your Lord,” and I was a witness over them so long as I was among them; when Thou didst take me up, Thou wert the Watcher over them; and Thou art witness over all things.\nاِنْ تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(118)\nIN TUA’AZZEBHUM FA INNAHUM E’EBAADUKA WA TAGHFER LAHUM FA-INNAKA ANTA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nShould Thou chastise them, Verily they are Thy servants; and should Thou forgive them, Verily Thou art the Mighty the Wise.\nقَالَ اللّٰهُ هٰذَا يَوْمُ يَنْفَعُ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ صِدْقُهُمْ‌ؕ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا‌ ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(119)\nQAALA LAAHO HAAZAA YAWMUD YANFAU’N SAADEQEENA SEDQUHUM LAHUM LAHUM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WARAZOOA A’NHO ZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nGod will say: “This is the day when shall benefit the truthful ones; their truth for them shall be gardens beneath which rivers flow to abide therein for ever; God is well pleased with them and they are well pleased with God; This is the great achievement.\nلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا فِيْهِنَّ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(120)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA FEEHINNA WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nGod’s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and what (all) is in them; and He (alone) hath the power over all things.",
  "merits": "There are 120 verses in this Surah and it is a ‘Makki’ Surah i.e. it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah, he will get a reward equivalent to ten times the number of Jews and Christians alive in the world, and will be forgiven the same amount of sins and will be raised in status by the same amount."
